 "readme": "# DTFH Task T5.3\n\nThis repository contains reproducible experiments for missing data imputation and\nbias correction on the UCI Heart Disease dataset.\n\n## What's Included\n\n- `dtfh_t5_3.py`: runnable experiments for\n  - imputation comparisons (mean/median/most-frequent/zero/KNN/CTGAN/TVAE)\n  - bias correction using synthetic data and fairness metrics\n- `results/`: generated plots and CSVs (created when you run the script)\n\n## Setup\n\nCreate a virtual environment and install dependencies:\n\n```bash\npython -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\nOr use conda:\n\n```bash\nconda env create -f environment.yml\nconda activate dtfh-t53\n```\n\n## Run\n\nImputation experiments:\n\n```bash\npython dtfh_t5_3.py --task imputation --output-dir results\n```\n\nBias correction experiments:\n\n```bash\npython dtfh_t5_3.py --task bias --output-dir results\n```\n\nRun everything:\n\n```bash\npython dtfh_t5_3.py --task all --output-dir results\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- The dataset is pulled from the UCI Heart Disease CSV hosted on GitHub.\n- Results (plots and CSVs) are saved into the output directory you provide.\n# dtfh_t53\n",
